## Original Problem
Current AudioWorklet implementation doesn't use transferable objects for buffer copying. Browser reuses audio buffers, causing data corruption.

## Fix (if needed for Option C/D)
```javascript
// audioProcessor.ts
class AudioProcessor extends AudioWorkletProcessor {
  process(inputs, outputs, parameters) {
    const input = inputs[0];
    if (input.length > 0) {
      const channel = input[0];
      // CRITICAL: Copy before posting - browser reuses the buffer
      const copy = new Float32Array(channel);
      this.port.postMessage(copy, [copy.buffer]); // Transfer ownership
    }
    return true;
  }
}
```

